  "question": {
    "text": "Let the maximum and minimum values of $\\left(\\sqrt{8 x-x^2-12}-4\\right)^2+(x-7)^2, x \\in \\mathbf{R}$ be $\\mathrm{M}$ and $\\mathrm{m}$, respectively. Then $\\mathrm{M}^2-\\mathrm{m}^2$ is equal to _________",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "1600",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & (x-7)^2+(y-4)^2 \\\\ & y=\\sqrt{8 x-x^2-12} \\\\ & y^2=-(x-4)^2+16-12 \\\\ & (x-4)^2+y^2=4\\end{aligned}$\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/WThTaKogzydNS5UDsgHmZqwudoBaGE_WTmt-oflPaBE.original.fullsize.png\"><br />$\\begin{aligned} & m=9 \\\\ & M=41 \\\\ & M^2-m^2=41^2-9^2=1600\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
